        "She waits the way she waited over the first pour, a woman who has already decided that your choice will be useful. The city goes on being melancholy on a timer. Your mouth tastes like cracked glass or like the name you sold or like a no you have not said yet.\n\n\"Inner room,\" she says, helpful, cruel. \"Or the south lift. I will not chase you down the corridor. Chasing is for Maren. I only invoice.\"\n\nThe second door is a darker mouth than last night. The ice is new. The lens is ready to be unsmoked. You can still refuse the sex and keep the rest of the leash for later. You can take the tape now and make the clinic a tomorrow problem. You can, if you have not already, invent the yes and see whether invention feels like power.",
        "Your body has opinions it was not asked for: the thigh that remembers her palm, the lip that remembers a thumb, the ribs that may be counting Radek. None of those opinions are a choice. They are weather. Crowe is weather too, and she has admitted it.\n\n\"If you come in,\" she adds, softer, which is not kinder, \"I will not pretend it is love. I will make it good enough that you cannot tell the story as only violence. That is the last mercy in the billing category. Afterward we will speak of Vale and the gala like people putting on coats. I keep that promise until it becomes leverage. You know the rest of the sentence.\" Hearing is not accepting. The second door is a darker mouth. Your ribs, if they count Radek, are weather. She is weather too. She has admitted it.",
